// An alias of an 'rc' reference taken under an enrichment's name is one more
// holder, counted as an alias under the same name is.
//
// An enrichment and its base share one representation, so the reference crosses
// between the two names in a recast (a CastNode with no FlagConvert). Flow asks
// flowIsLvalRead whether the value it hands over still has a holder behind it,
// and that looked only through a name, field, index or dereference: the recast
// read as a temporary, the alias added no holder, and both names released one at
// scope exit -- a count taken to zero while 'plain' still pointed at it.
//
// A run cannot show this: the read after the early free reads what the freed
// block still holds, and the second release decrements freed memory without
// freeing it again. The check is on the count itself.

mod region_enrich_count;

struct Plain {
  pub n i32;
}

struct RichPlain extends Plain {
  pub fn doubled(self &) i32 { n * 2; }
}

fn aliasAcross() {
  imm plain = +rc-mut Plain[54];
  imm rich +rc-mut RichPlain = plain;
}
